.SH NAME
set \- establish or modify a C Shell variable
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBset \fR[\fIname\fB=\fIvalue\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without an argument, the set command
command shows the value of all shell variables.
Variables that have other than a single word as value print as a word
list enclosed in parentheses.
.PP
The \fBset\fR command with
an argument in the form \fIname\fB=\fIvalue\fR,
\fBset\fR sets
.I name
to the single
.I value
.PP
Variable expansion happens for all arguments before any
setting occurs.
.SH SEE ALSO
csh(1), env(1), printenv(1), setenv(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
